1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:14,926 --> 00:00:16,640
But I really don't want to go home.

9
00:00:16,707 --> 00:00:19,720
Why don't you stay here with me for one night?

10
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,440
I'll let you go wherever you want.

11
00:00:21,481 --> 00:00:23,000
Except to see that woman.

12
00:00:23,082 --> 00:00:24,720
Throw that away. I'll buy you a new one.

13
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,960
You're so mean! I hate you when you're like this!

14
00:00:27,054 --> 00:00:30,920
- Who taught you to talk like that?
- You wicked mother!

15
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:32,788
Titus! Titus!

16
00:00:33,339 --> 00:00:36,720
This is what I'll use to prove that Nopnapha ordered my sister's murder.

17
00:00:36,747 --> 00:00:38,840
I've already gotten close to her younger child.

18
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:40,974
Now I'll find a way to get close to the older one.

19
00:00:41,064 --> 00:00:42,480
I'm sure I'll uncover plenty more useful information.

20
00:00:42,547 --> 00:00:45,600
Munin, I signed the Smart Card project contract today.

21
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:49,000
But weren't you planning to sabotage the project
to ruin Nopnapha's reputation?

22
00:00:49,031 --> 00:00:51,320
If she goes down, we go down with her.

23
00:00:51,366 --> 00:00:54,200
I promise I won't put our company at risk.

24
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:57,120
Get this phone checked for Nopnapha's fingerprints.

25
00:00:57,611 --> 00:00:59,240
The fingerprint results are back.

26
00:00:59,376 --> 00:01:01,520
There's no trace of Nopnapha's fingerprints!

27
00:01:01,678 --> 00:01:02,880
Then whose fingerprints are on it?

28
00:01:03,016 --> 00:01:05,560
Jenphop's. His are the only fingerprints on it.

29
00:01:05,859 --> 00:01:09,060
The phone belongs to Jenphop, not Nopnapha.

30
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,801
Munin!

31
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:14,120
You've been going after the wrong person all along!

32
00:01:17,238 --> 00:01:19,040
Is the fried chicken good, sweetie?

33
00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:22,320
It's delicious, Mom! Can you make it for me every day?

34
00:01:22,451 --> 00:01:23,600
Of course, sweetheart.

35
00:01:23,891 --> 00:01:27,491
Hurry up and finish eating. Daddy will take you to the mall afterward.

36
00:01:27,518 --> 00:01:30,280
Yay! I love Mom and Dad more than anything.

37
00:01:34,192 --> 00:01:36,193
You kids are always playing make-believe.

38
00:01:37,974 --> 00:01:40,320
Families like that don't exist in real life.

39
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:43,760
If they did, would you two be sitting here playing with trash?

40
00:01:45,878 --> 00:01:49,320
You crazy old hag! Just because you can't find a husband
doesn't mean you have to run your mouth!

41
00:01:49,611 --> 00:01:51,880
You little brat, Nin! Watch your filthy mouth!

42
00:01:54,342 --> 00:01:56,000
Why the hell did you slap me?

43
00:01:56,118 --> 00:01:57,119
You crazy little bitch!

44
00:02:03,048 --> 00:02:05,360
You're no match for me, you little orphan brat!

45
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:07,440
Even your parents don't love you!

46
00:02:08,035 --> 00:02:12,000
You'll never have the happy family you've always dreamed of!

47
00:02:12,318 --> 00:02:13,319
Mark my words!

48
00:02:23,319 --> 00:02:25,280
Ta, don't listen to her.

49
00:02:25,424 --> 00:02:28,600
When we grow up, we'll get married and have kids.

50
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,246
And we'll build happy, loving families, Ta.

51
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:34,051
We'll build houses right next to each other.

52
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:36,760
And our kids can play together too.

53
00:02:36,779 --> 00:02:37,780
Yeah.

54
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,712
Do you really think these two things are connected?

55
00:04:08,566 --> 00:04:09,567
It's possible.

56
00:04:11,046 --> 00:04:14,123
My sister got pregnant, and the Director told her to have an abortion.

57
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:15,861
Ta refused.

58
00:04:16,875 --> 00:04:17,876
So he ordered her killed.

59
00:04:19,739 --> 00:04:21,720
When you first went back to see the Director,

60
00:04:22,326 --> 00:04:25,170
did he seem shocked or surprised at all?

61
00:04:32,672 --> 00:04:33,673
Oh.

62
00:04:34,491 --> 00:04:35,600
You're back at work?

63
00:04:36,235 --> 00:04:37,600
Yes, Director.

64
00:04:40,683 --> 00:04:42,619
He didn't seem particularly surprised.

65
00:04:43,787 --> 00:04:46,080
When I talked to him alone in his office,

66
00:04:46,683 --> 00:04:48,920
he didn't show any signs of having ordered Ta's murder.

67
00:04:51,886 --> 00:04:53,520
Or maybe he's just really good at hiding it.

68
00:04:53,966 --> 00:04:55,520
When he found out the killer had failed,

69
00:04:55,608 --> 00:04:57,640
he might've pretended nothing had happened.

70
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,000
But he did ask about the pregnancy.

71
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,040
He even seemed concerned about Ta's miscarriage.

72
00:05:08,544 --> 00:05:11,680
Didn't your sister mention her pregnancy or miscarriage in her diary?

73
00:05:17,542 --> 00:05:20,520
If she didn't write everything down,

74
00:05:21,670 --> 00:05:25,840
there could be a lot more about her that we don't know.

75
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:29,080
Are you saying

76
00:05:30,648 --> 00:05:32,240
my sister might've had trouble with someone else,

77
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:35,400
besides Nopnapha and Jenphop?

78
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:40,376
Yeah, it's possible.

79
00:05:43,304 --> 00:05:45,200
I'm just saying we should consider every possibility.

80
00:05:46,464 --> 00:05:49,019
Her diary doesn't tell us everything about her life.

81
00:05:53,211 --> 00:05:55,046
Looks like we'll have to dig even deeper from now on

82
00:05:55,952 --> 00:05:57,300
and stop jumping to conclusions.

83
00:05:59,334 --> 00:06:01,100
I don't want to take revenge on the wrong person.

84
00:06:06,123 --> 00:06:07,867
But based on the clues we have so far,

85
00:06:10,059 --> 00:06:11,520
our prime suspect

86
00:06:12,566 --> 00:06:13,640
is Jenphop.

87
00:06:25,567 --> 00:06:26,568
Stop.

88
00:06:28,104 --> 00:06:29,120
The Minister wants to see you.

89
00:06:30,366 --> 00:06:32,967
Apparently, she wants to thank you for looking after Titus last night.

90
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,501
No thanks necessary.

91
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,960
Just consider it an act of charity for a lousy mother.

92
00:06:37,283 --> 00:06:38,560
- I'm not going.
- Hey!

93
00:06:39,486 --> 00:06:41,614
Who the hell do you think you are?

94
00:06:42,323 --> 00:06:44,250
Don't get too full of yourself. Come with me.

95
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:47,320
You're just a lackey. No need to act so tough.

96
00:06:48,144 --> 00:06:50,920
Go tell your boss I'm not coming.

97
00:06:51,838 --> 00:06:53,600
Are you coming willingly, or do I have to drag you by the hair?

98
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:55,960
I'm not scared of you. I've got fists and feet too, you know.

99
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,241
You bitch, Mutta!

100
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:03,056
What do you want, Nopnapha?

101
00:07:08,123 --> 00:07:10,920
Stop Director Jenphop and Veekit right now.

102
00:07:10,987 --> 00:07:12,560
Yes, of course.

103
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,760
Chuenchom, Mrs. Nopnapha's about to slap Mutta again.

104
00:07:18,536 --> 00:07:20,180
We have to keep Veekit away.

105
00:07:26,232 --> 00:07:27,960
Pee standing up like a real man.

106
00:07:29,539 --> 00:07:31,240
Want to pee together, Veekit?

107
00:07:33,043 --> 00:07:34,160
I'm here to take a dump.

108
00:07:41,966 --> 00:07:44,131
Being a man must be so convenient.

109
00:07:44,376 --> 00:07:46,130
Just give it a little shake, and you're all clean.

110
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,501
Hey!

111
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,001
- What's that?
- What's that?

112
00:08:08,872 --> 00:08:09,873
What's going on?

113
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,501
Hey!

114
00:08:16,158 --> 00:08:17,250
Get your camera ready, you old hag!

115
00:08:27,587 --> 00:08:29,500
- Hello, sir.
- Hey! Why are you blocking the way?

116
00:08:29,811 --> 00:08:31,012
Do you know who I am?

117
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:34,328
There's an eight-meter-deep sinkhole up ahead, sir.

118
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,558
If you fall in, you're as good as dead.

119
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:38,209
Please go this way instead.

120
00:08:40,147 --> 00:08:41,148
Let's go that way. Come on.

121
00:08:45,496 --> 00:08:48,160
We really have a knack for sticking our noses into things.

122
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:51,900
We always show up just in time for a historic moment.

123
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:52,921
Yeah.

124
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,400
No filming, please.

125
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:59,741
Today, Mrs. Nopnapha is about to slap that shameless bitch Mutta again!

126
00:09:00,094 --> 00:09:01,095
Go ahead, ma'am.

127
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:04,101
It's been months since you last got slapped.

128
00:09:04,814 --> 00:09:06,415
You must miss the sting of my hand.

129
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:08,520
I'll give you another taste.

130
00:09:09,376 --> 00:09:12,240
Consider it my way of thanking you for taking such good care of my daughter.

131
00:09:17,631 --> 00:09:18,622
You bitch!

132
00:09:18,628 --> 00:09:20,480
What an idiot! Go grab her by the hair!

133
00:09:20,996 --> 00:09:21,997
Get over here!

134
00:09:43,043 --> 00:09:45,640
Grandpa's hair, Grandma's hair, everyone's hair!

135
00:09:46,379 --> 00:09:48,380
Do you even have any real hair, Mutta?

136
00:09:48,651 --> 00:09:50,252
I bet your whole head is fake, you bitch!

137
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,200
You'd even let yourself get hurt to please your boss.

138
00:09:52,806 --> 00:09:54,520
I hope she gives you a raise.

139
00:09:54,807 --> 00:09:55,808
You filthy lowlife!

140
00:09:56,872 --> 00:09:58,073
A legendary slap like this?

141
00:09:59,214 --> 00:10:00,920
I've got to see it up close!

142
00:10:02,190 --> 00:10:03,680
- Hurry up!
- I'm coming!

143
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:07,701
You bitch, Mutta!

144
00:10:07,768 --> 00:10:10,040
You keep calling my name! What, is it your mother's name too?

145
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,551
Ouch! That was savage!

146
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:18,151
Who locked the door?

147
00:10:19,496 --> 00:10:21,920
Is anyone out there? Can someone open the door?

148
00:10:23,541 --> 00:10:24,600
Hello? Is anyone out there?

149
00:10:25,723 --> 00:10:28,240
- Please open the door!
- Hurry! Mrs. Nopnapha's about to slap that homewrecking bitch again!

150
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:29,920
Seriously? Let's go!

151
00:10:30,251 --> 00:10:31,252
Ta!

152
00:10:31,739 --> 00:10:33,640
Help! Someone open the door!

153
00:10:34,214 --> 00:10:35,766
Shit! What the hell?

154
00:10:40,827 --> 00:10:41,828
That's what happens when you get old.

155
00:10:42,923 --> 00:10:43,960
You've got quite a mouth on you, bitch!

156
00:10:57,838 --> 00:10:59,280
Everyone, take a good look at this woman!

157
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:03,080
She thinks she can abuse anyone just because she's powerful.

158
00:11:03,606 --> 00:11:06,440
Today, someone who was once her victim is fighting back!

159
00:11:06,683 --> 00:11:07,684
Open the damn door!

160
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,361
Ta!

161
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,280
I won't let history repeat itself.

162
00:11:13,851 --> 00:11:15,280
These steps outside the Ministry

163
00:11:15,872 --> 00:11:17,873
are going to taste your filthy blood for a change.

164
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,001
Everyone.

165
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:37,240
Mrs. Nopnapha's coming! Move!

166
00:11:45,894 --> 00:11:46,895
Is she going to die?

167
00:11:46,966 --> 00:11:50,000
Mutta! You slapped me!

168
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,921
You're going to die a horrible death!

169
00:11:52,630 --> 00:11:55,080
No, you're the one who's going to die a horrible death.

170
00:12:24,470 --> 00:12:25,840
Let me wash your face for you.

171
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,461
So you can pass on to a better afterlife.

172
00:12:33,366 --> 00:12:34,440
Congratulations!

173
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:38,196
The legendary slap outside the Ministry will go down in history

174
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:39,960
with your name instead of Mutta's.

175
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,061
Give it back!

176
00:12:52,462 --> 00:12:53,463
What?

177
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:54,680
My hairpiece!

178
00:12:55,398 --> 00:12:56,699
Look at all these split ends!

179
00:12:57,718 --> 00:13:00,040
You really should get a hair treatment. Here!

180
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:10,660
Napha, why are you lying on the ground?

181
00:13:13,214 --> 00:13:15,963
That bitch Mutta slapped me down the stairs.

182
00:13:16,662 --> 00:13:18,680
Come help me up. I'm in so much pain.

183
00:13:19,552 --> 00:13:20,553
Whoa!

184
00:13:20,710 --> 00:13:22,711
I can't. I've got a bad back.

185
00:13:23,062 --> 00:13:25,728
Hey, Thaithat! Call an ambulance!

186
00:13:25,995 --> 00:13:27,560
Tell them it's urgent! It's an emergency.

187
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,901
Hey!

188
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:34,774
What are you all staring at?

189
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:36,400
Come on, move along!

190
00:13:37,446 --> 00:13:39,480
The show's over. Get back to work!

191
00:13:39,664 --> 00:13:41,165
It was just getting good.

192
00:13:43,721 --> 00:13:45,480
That was brutal, I'm telling you.

193
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,801
Uncle Phop.

194
00:13:50,584 --> 00:13:52,560
Do you really think someone can change that much?

195
00:13:54,406 --> 00:13:56,520
Ta's like a completely different person now.

196
00:13:59,432 --> 00:14:01,880
Hey, isn't that a good thing?

197
00:14:03,374 --> 00:14:05,400
Now Napha won't dare mess with her again.

198
00:14:11,398 --> 00:14:12,399
Yes, please.

199
00:14:13,366 --> 00:14:15,567
I'd like some bright, colorful flowers.

200
00:14:17,472 --> 00:14:18,473
Thank you.

201
00:14:23,915 --> 00:14:26,416
Hong, where is everyone?

202
00:14:28,248 --> 00:14:30,280
They're downstairs gossiping.

203
00:14:31,672 --> 00:14:34,142
Want to know what they're saying, Ta?

204
00:14:34,482 --> 00:14:35,483
No.

205
00:14:39,168 --> 00:14:40,600
They're saying

206
00:14:41,584 --> 00:14:44,600
being the Director's mistress is bad enough,

207
00:14:45,312 --> 00:14:47,640
but slapping his wife down the stairs

208
00:14:48,272 --> 00:14:50,683
makes you a hundred times worse.

209
00:14:51,936 --> 00:14:55,720
Your name should go down in Thailand's history books

210
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,520
as the most vicious mistress of all time.

211
00:15:00,539 --> 00:15:01,560
Who said that?

212
00:15:03,094 --> 00:15:04,640
I don't really know.

213
00:15:05,136 --> 00:15:08,440
I just overheard bits and pieces. I wasn't really listening.

214
00:15:10,936 --> 00:15:13,120
But everyone seems to agree

215
00:15:13,443 --> 00:15:15,121
that they're on the wife's side.

216
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,920
Nobody's siding with the mistress.

217
00:15:18,881 --> 00:15:21,000
And whose side are you on, Hong?

218
00:15:25,627 --> 00:15:27,240
The mistress's side, of course.

219
00:15:28,422 --> 00:15:32,360
Because I'm on your side, Ta.

220
00:15:33,072 --> 00:15:34,073
You got this.

221
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,501
[You bitch!]

222
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:01,880
Nopnapha's and Oshi's X-ray results are both normal.

223
00:16:02,115 --> 00:16:04,160
But you may have some minor sprains.

224
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:05,731
So I've put you in soft casts for now.

225
00:16:05,976 --> 00:16:08,500
You can take them off once you're feeling better.

226
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:11,250
- Thank you, Doctor.
- Thank you.

227
00:16:11,416 --> 00:16:12,417
Excuse me.

228
00:16:14,568 --> 00:16:16,800
I'm sorry I didn't get back in time to help you, ma'am.

229
00:16:17,952 --> 00:16:19,739
Oshi, what were you doing?

230
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:21,648
I was helping her.

231
00:16:22,182 --> 00:16:23,800
She told me to strike first.

232
00:16:24,019 --> 00:16:25,020
And look what happened.

233
00:16:25,446 --> 00:16:28,047
I struck first, and now we're both swollen.

234
00:16:29,456 --> 00:16:31,232
You've made sure to keep this out of the news, right?

235
00:16:31,691 --> 00:16:33,520
I've already secured the CCTV footage.

236
00:16:35,947 --> 00:16:38,700
Hello, I've got a delivery.

237
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,840
- Could you sign for it, please?
- Sure.

238
00:16:44,624 --> 00:16:45,880
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

239
00:16:54,211 --> 00:16:55,480
How thoughtful!

240
00:16:55,838 --> 00:16:58,270
Sending an electric fan instead of flowers to someone in the hospital.

241
00:16:58,872 --> 00:17:01,120
At least it's useful. I'll turn it on.

242
00:17:07,561 --> 00:17:09,480
Such a cool breeze.

243
00:17:09,782 --> 00:17:11,880
And it smells so fresh.

244
00:17:12,027 --> 00:17:14,328
Even though the flowers are fake.

245
00:17:17,467 --> 00:17:20,368
Sorry, there's something else. I forgot to attach it.

246
00:17:23,147 --> 00:17:24,648
There you go. Thank you.

247
00:17:27,238 --> 00:17:30,039
"With love and wicked wishes,

248
00:17:30,995 --> 00:17:32,480
Hope you die soon.

249
00:17:33,755 --> 00:17:34,756
From Mutta."

250
00:17:38,742 --> 00:17:41,734
Oshi, get a hitman to shoot that bitch right now!

251
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,624
We can't do that, ma'am.

252
00:17:43,928 --> 00:17:45,680
We can't take risks like that anymore.

253
00:17:46,083 --> 00:17:47,864
If word gets out, it won't be worth it.

254
00:17:48,782 --> 00:17:52,174
Will you stop telling me what I can and can't do?

255
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,350
It's your job to make sure nothing gets out.

256
00:17:57,432 --> 00:17:59,800
She's stealing my husband and my children!

257
00:17:59,859 --> 00:18:01,280
She slapped me down the stairs!

258
00:18:01,358 --> 00:18:04,600
And now she's sent me a funeral wreath fan to humiliate me!

259
00:18:05,192 --> 00:18:08,193
If I let her get away with this, don't call me Nopnapha.

260
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,480
I'm not saying you shouldn't deal with her, ma'am.

261
00:18:12,931 --> 00:18:14,560
I'm just suggesting we find a way to do it through proper channels,

262
00:18:15,134 --> 00:18:16,960
so you won't have to put yourself at risk.

263
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:29,107
You had to cause trouble again this morning?

264
00:18:30,392 --> 00:18:32,147
Nopnapha was the one who picked a fight with me.

265
00:18:32,159 --> 00:18:34,660
But you slapped her so hard she went tumbling down the stairs.

266
00:18:35,787 --> 00:18:38,059
And what about what happened at my house?

267
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:41,561
You were the one who barged into my home.

268
00:18:41,627 --> 00:18:43,000
You started it, Ta.

269
00:18:43,488 --> 00:18:45,050
And do you know what's happened now?

270
00:18:45,459 --> 00:18:47,438
My daughter is insulting her own mother.

271
00:18:49,347 --> 00:18:51,048
That's because she treats her daughter badly.

272
00:18:51,614 --> 00:18:53,260
How is that my fault?

273
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,940
Maybe not directly, but indirectly, Ta.

274
00:18:55,651 --> 00:18:58,280
If you hadn't gotten involved with Titus, none of this would've happened.

275
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:00,551
Listen.

276
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:04,040
I'm warning you.

277
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:06,600
Stay away from Titus.

278
00:19:08,278 --> 00:19:10,279
And don't you ever set foot in my house again.

279
00:19:13,339 --> 00:19:16,160
Just because I love you doesn't mean I'll let you get away with everything, Ta.

280
00:19:17,424 --> 00:19:19,160
If you don't listen to me,

281
00:19:22,358 --> 00:19:24,560
I'll show you a side of me you've never seen before.

282
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:54,901
Is that offer to take me out for dim sum still open?

283
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,730
I've figured out why I never liked dim sum.

284
00:20:34,552 --> 00:20:36,803
I just haven't found a good place yet.

285
00:20:37,064 --> 00:20:38,880
Do you really like it?

286
00:20:40,424 --> 00:20:41,450
You're not just forcing yourself, are you?

287
00:20:44,158 --> 00:20:45,159
You're not just forcing yourself, are you?

288
00:20:47,928 --> 00:20:50,120
If you don't like it, you don't have to pretend.

289
00:20:50,558 --> 00:20:51,559
When you're with me,

290
00:20:52,862 --> 00:20:56,080
you don't have to be anyone else. Just be yourself, one hundred percent.

291
00:20:57,731 --> 00:20:59,170
I am being one hundred percent myself.

292
00:20:59,630 --> 00:21:00,631
I'm Mutta.

293
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:07,161
But the Mutta I knew wasn't like this.

294
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,920
Every day, we die and are reborn in a way.

295
00:21:12,601 --> 00:21:15,602
The Mutta you used to know is dead.

296
00:21:16,131 --> 00:21:18,960
The person sitting next to you now is someone else.

297
00:21:19,958 --> 00:21:21,559
Please accept the new me, Veekit.

298
00:21:25,142 --> 00:21:26,950
I'll try to understand what you're saying.

299
00:21:33,611 --> 00:21:34,612
It's Uncle Phop calling.

300
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:38,901
Hello?

301
00:21:40,854 --> 00:21:43,855
Oh, I've already called the staff. They should be there this afternoon.

302
00:21:48,027 --> 00:21:50,028
I'll head over as soon as I finish eating.

303
00:21:52,955 --> 00:21:54,800
He scraped his car against a pole.

304
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,520
So I had to call the insurance company for him.

305
00:21:59,267 --> 00:22:02,560
Does he make you handle everything whenever he has a problem?

306
00:22:04,627 --> 00:22:07,080
Yeah. I'm technically his secretary,

307
00:22:08,062 --> 00:22:09,200
but I'm also his nephew.

308
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:12,601
So he keeps finding excuses to make me do things for him.

309
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:16,880
Including illegal things?

310
00:22:17,494 --> 00:22:18,495
What do you mean?

311
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,201
What are you getting at?

312
00:22:22,214 --> 00:22:25,800
Veekit, if you're sincere with me, tell me the truth.

313
00:22:28,032 --> 00:22:29,733
Has he ever made you do anything shady?

314
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:32,320
What kind of shady things?

315
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,560
What are you trying to say, Ta?

316
00:22:35,115 --> 00:22:36,400
Just tell me straight.

317
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:42,001
Has he ever tried to hurt or kill anyone?

318
00:22:42,224 --> 00:22:43,225
Hey!

319
00:22:45,174 --> 00:22:46,340
Why are you asking me that?

320
00:22:48,966 --> 00:22:49,967
Just answer me, Veekit.

321
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:51,501
Never.

322
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:54,540
He's never asked me to do anything like that.

323
00:22:54,984 --> 00:22:56,485
And even if he did, I wouldn't do it.

324
00:22:57,838 --> 00:22:59,845
As for whether he's done anything himself, I don't know.

325
00:23:01,798 --> 00:23:03,440
Now it's your turn.

326
00:23:04,326 --> 00:23:05,627
Tell me what's going on.

327
00:23:08,475 --> 00:23:11,315
Nothing. I was just curious.

328
00:23:11,651 --> 00:23:14,080
I'm just worried that if I ever upset him,

329
00:23:14,398 --> 00:23:16,081
he might send someone to hurt me.

330
00:23:26,027 --> 00:23:29,690
According to our survey, our ministry is overstaffed.

331
00:23:30,832 --> 00:23:34,133
Some departments have dozens of employees, but only five actually work.

332
00:23:35,059 --> 00:23:37,460
The rest just sit around waiting for lunch every day.

333
00:23:37,918 --> 00:23:39,520
I've already spoken to the Civil Service Commission

334
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:43,440
about cutting unnecessary positions.

335
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,512
No way! I'm not resigning, no matter what!

336
00:23:55,608 --> 00:23:58,240
I've worked here for 20 years. That department head position should be mine!

337
00:23:58,309 --> 00:23:59,310
I'm not leaving!

338
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:01,600
I'm not leaving either, Toey!

339
00:24:01,912 --> 00:24:03,200
Oh, come on! I've been working here...

340
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:06,000
What about all those files, documents, and papers?
They're so heavy! Who's going to carry them?

341
00:24:06,067 --> 00:24:08,000
These people can't even lift them.

342
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:10,936
I paid 300,000 baht just to pass the civil service exam.

343
00:24:10,974 --> 00:24:13,819
I haven't even earned that money back yet. I'm not leaving.

344
00:24:13,862 --> 00:24:15,400
I'm not leaving either, Toey.

345
00:24:15,446 --> 00:24:18,440
If you fire me, I'll come scream in the cafeteria every day

346
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:20,520
until you give me my job back.

347
00:24:20,822 --> 00:24:24,000
As for me, I'm smart, handsome,

348
00:24:24,163 --> 00:24:25,440
and talented.

349
00:24:25,886 --> 00:24:27,840
And most importantly, I'm a straight man.

350
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:31,201
All I know how to do is make photocopies.

351
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:34,601
If you fire me, how am I supposed to make a living?

352
00:24:34,601 --> 00:24:37,280
Then fire her. All she does is make photocopies anyway.

353
00:24:40,147 --> 00:24:41,480
Oh, stop it!

354
00:24:42,835 --> 00:24:44,200
Can you all stop panicking?

355
00:24:45,715 --> 00:24:48,080
They're not firing everyone, just two people.

356
00:24:54,278 --> 00:24:55,400
Hey, quiet!

357
00:24:59,190 --> 00:25:00,720
As for who's going to be let go,

358
00:25:00,843 --> 00:25:02,800
I've been put in charge of deciding.

359
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:04,801
You all have one month

360
00:25:05,301 --> 00:25:06,680
to prove yourselves

361
00:25:06,702 --> 00:25:08,300
and show why you deserve to stay.

362
00:25:10,542 --> 00:25:11,543
I'm sorry.

363
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,601
I really don't want to do this.

364
00:25:14,467 --> 00:25:16,920
But the official order has been issued, so I have to follow it.

365
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:21,761
Toey.

366
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,520
I'm one of the two

367
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:26,921
who has to go, right?

368
00:25:29,307 --> 00:25:31,320
Just tell me. I can take it.

369
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:36,860
Toey, you know who you need to fire.

370
00:25:37,955 --> 00:25:39,464
You mean Mutta, ma'am?

371
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:45,180
It's the only way to put an end to the scandal in our ministry.

372
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:48,801
You care about this ministry, don't you?

373
00:25:49,501 --> 00:25:50,502
Yeah.

374
00:25:58,027 --> 00:26:00,027
Don't worry, Ta.

375
00:26:00,176 --> 00:26:02,177
You can join my insurance sales team.

376
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:04,600
With looks like yours, you'll sell policies like hotcakes.

377
00:26:06,374 --> 00:26:09,616
Everyone, let this be a lesson to you.

378
00:26:10,459 --> 00:26:14,160
If you want to get ahead, work hard at your desk,

379
00:26:14,518 --> 00:26:16,360
not in someone else's bed.

380
00:26:18,438 --> 00:26:20,480
I warned you before, you know.

381
00:26:20,795 --> 00:26:22,640
But you just kept acting all high and mighty.

382
00:26:22,912 --> 00:26:24,080
And look where that got you.

383
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:25,701
Game over!

384
00:26:26,128 --> 00:26:30,619
Ta, when are you packing up your things? Just let me know.

385
00:26:30,752 --> 00:26:33,000
I've got plenty of cardboard boxes at home.

386
00:26:33,046 --> 00:26:34,600
I drink a lot of beer, you see.

387
00:26:35,247 --> 00:26:38,480
Have you decided where you want your farewell party?

388
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:43,040
Just let me know. I'll book a place for you.

389
00:26:48,019 --> 00:26:49,120
Everyone,

390
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:51,360
please stop rubbing salt in Ta's wounds.

391
00:26:52,542 --> 00:26:54,120
She just made a bad choice

392
00:26:54,467 --> 00:26:56,168
by having an affair with the Director.

393
00:26:57,176 --> 00:26:59,544
Now that she's being fired from the civil service,

394
00:26:59,587 --> 00:27:02,480
I'm sure she'll learn her lesson and change her ways.

395
00:27:03,091 --> 00:27:05,960
She probably won't dare go after another woman's husband again.

396
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:12,680
Ta, I really don't know what to say, so...

397
00:27:13,827 --> 00:27:15,128
I guess I won't say anything.

398
00:27:20,019 --> 00:27:24,040
I think you should all worry about yourselves instead.

399
00:27:24,526 --> 00:27:27,080
At least I know my fate, so I can relax.

400
00:27:27,886 --> 00:27:31,920
I won't have to spend the next month worrying myself sick.

401
00:27:32,331 --> 00:27:33,800
It's the rest of you

402
00:27:34,176 --> 00:27:37,160
who'll have to fight to impress Toey.

403
00:27:38,374 --> 00:27:40,040
I wonder

404
00:27:42,152 --> 00:27:44,153
who'll be joining me on the way out.

405
00:28:05,488 --> 00:28:07,000
Getting fired is a good thing.

406
00:28:07,262 --> 00:28:09,263
Now you can finally work here full-time.

407
00:28:10,263 --> 00:28:11,264
See?

408
00:28:11,300 --> 00:28:13,601
I've hired more people to help us code the Smart Card system.

409
00:28:17,158 --> 00:28:19,359
But that means I'll have fewer chances to see Jenphop.

410
00:28:20,288 --> 00:28:23,320
It's much easier to run into him at the Ministry than outside.

411
00:28:25,289 --> 00:28:28,382
Oh, have you talked to Veekit yet?

412
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:30,001
Did you find out anything?

413
00:28:30,179 --> 00:28:33,240
I did, but I haven't learned anything new.

414
00:28:33,859 --> 00:28:35,320
I've only just realized

415
00:28:35,646 --> 00:28:37,880
that he has a nasty temper too.

416
00:28:38,478 --> 00:28:39,720
Because when I talked to Veekit,

417
00:28:39,923 --> 00:28:42,960
he said he'd never helped Jenphop do anything seriously wrong.

418
00:28:43,816 --> 00:28:44,817
Who knows?

419
00:28:45,918 --> 00:28:48,019
The uncle and nephew might be working together.

420
00:28:48,300 --> 00:28:49,301
How can we trust him?

421
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:51,521
True.

422
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:53,920
But I have someone else in mind

423
00:28:54,601 --> 00:28:56,800
who can give us inside information on Jenphop.

424
00:28:58,370 --> 00:28:59,371
Who?

425
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:00,721
Tetris.

426
00:29:00,821 --> 00:29:01,822
Huh?

427
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:04,032
You're going after both of his children?

428
00:29:04,464 --> 00:29:07,165
I've talked to Titus. She's still too young.

429
00:29:07,312 --> 00:29:08,747
She doesn't know much about what the adults are up to.

430
00:29:08,971 --> 00:29:12,572
But Tetris seems to know everything about his parents' problems.

431
00:29:12,972 --> 00:29:14,560
How are you going to talk to him?

432
00:29:14,864 --> 00:29:17,665
Didn't you say he couldn't stand you?

433
00:29:18,592 --> 00:29:22,320
Titus told me her brother likes chatting with guys on an app.

434
00:29:22,420 --> 00:29:23,760
His profile picture is a mermaid.

435
00:29:27,774 --> 00:29:28,775
Hi.

436
00:29:37,315 --> 00:29:38,800
Hi. What's your name?

437
00:29:39,550 --> 00:29:40,840
M. You?

438
00:29:42,099 --> 00:29:43,100
Wonyoung.

439
00:29:44,692 --> 00:29:46,360
Are there mermaids in Korea?

440
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:52,300
Doesn't your boyfriend mind you using this app?

441
00:29:53,739 --> 00:29:54,840
Are you asking if I'm single?

442
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:58,880
No, I'm just worried you might already have a boyfriend.

443
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:01,450
I'm single. We can chat.

444
00:30:02,251 --> 00:30:03,414
I'm single too.

445
00:30:04,070 --> 00:30:06,371
I'm sick of my family. Just looking for someone to talk to.

446
00:30:06,750 --> 00:30:08,151
I'm sick of mine too.

447
00:30:09,083 --> 00:30:10,084
Who are you sick of?

448
00:30:10,784 --> 00:30:13,180
My dad. He's a womanizer.

449
00:30:13,891 --> 00:30:15,320
Oh, same here!

450
00:30:15,571 --> 00:30:16,620
That's what all straight men are like.

451
00:30:18,478 --> 00:30:19,960
Looks like we're in the same boat.

452
00:30:20,184 --> 00:30:22,085
Wanna keep chatting?

453
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,901
Sure. First one to disappear loses.

454
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:28,101
You're on!

455
00:30:30,654 --> 00:30:32,088
I'll get close to Tetris

456
00:30:32,371 --> 00:30:33,920
and slowly trick him into revealing information.

457
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:37,360
Kids with troubled families need someone to confide in.

458
00:30:37,784 --> 00:30:41,747
He might end up telling a complete stranger everything.

459
00:30:50,790 --> 00:30:51,791
Let's go.

460
00:30:55,171 --> 00:30:56,172
Goodbye!

461
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:02,071
Tetris.

462
00:31:03,171 --> 00:31:04,172
Yes?

463
00:31:04,747 --> 00:31:05,840
We're at school.

464
00:31:07,748 --> 00:31:09,700
- Bye, Veekit!
- Wait, wait!

465
00:31:09,974 --> 00:31:12,760
Who are you chatting with? You've been on your phone since breakfast.

466
00:31:14,395 --> 00:31:15,396
Your boyfriend?

467
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:17,776
No, just a friend.

468
00:31:59,518 --> 00:32:00,600
Yeah, right. Like anyone would believe that.

469
00:32:00,904 --> 00:32:03,400
Just bumped into an alpaca at the Ministry.

470
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:05,801
I told you to call me Al Pacino!

471
00:32:07,251 --> 00:32:10,734
So who were you chatting with? You weren't even watching
where you were going.

472
00:32:11,616 --> 00:32:13,760
Well, why didn't you move if you saw me coming?

473
00:32:14,368 --> 00:32:16,100
Because I wanted you to bump into me so I could tease you.

474
00:32:18,283 --> 00:32:20,640
You and my uncle have one thing in common.

475
00:32:21,320 --> 00:32:22,480
You both flirt with every woman you meet.

476
00:32:23,851 --> 00:32:25,160
But there's one big difference.

477
00:32:25,296 --> 00:32:28,160
If I ever get married, I'd never cheat like my uncle.

478
00:32:29,531 --> 00:32:30,720
Is that your pickup line?

479
00:32:31,300 --> 00:32:32,301
That's so cringe.

480
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:36,414
Since when is being faithful cringe?

481
00:32:37,827 --> 00:32:40,640
Oh, or do you prefer bad boys like my uncle?

482
00:32:42,107 --> 00:32:44,800
Aren't you afraid Uncle Phop will come after you for talking to me like this?

483
00:32:45,510 --> 00:32:46,511
Not at all.

484
00:32:47,100 --> 00:32:48,101
Veekit!

485
00:32:54,950 --> 00:32:55,951
Hey!

486
00:32:57,150 --> 00:32:59,720
Don't you have anything better to do?

487
00:33:00,720 --> 00:33:03,960
If you don't have enough work, I'll find you more.

488
00:33:05,272 --> 00:33:08,718
No, sir. I was just saying hi to Ta as a friend.

489
00:33:09,283 --> 00:33:12,800
And flirting a little, since I'm single.

490
00:33:16,731 --> 00:33:17,880
Talk to you later, Ta.

491
00:33:21,968 --> 00:33:22,969
Excuse me.

492
00:33:29,707 --> 00:33:30,960
Was he flirting with you?

493
00:33:31,435 --> 00:33:32,436
Yes.

494
00:33:32,624 --> 00:33:35,760
He has been for a while, and he seems to be getting more serious.

495
00:33:36,488 --> 00:33:38,880
Then stop talking to him. I don't like it.

496
00:33:42,435 --> 00:33:43,950
And what if I don't?

497
00:33:45,918 --> 00:33:48,480
Ta, what's gotten into you lately?

498
00:33:49,963 --> 00:33:51,481
You've been provoking me over and over.

499
00:33:52,283 --> 00:33:54,160
Why can't you listen to me like you used to?

500
00:33:55,659 --> 00:33:57,440
I used to do everything you told me?

501
00:33:57,864 --> 00:33:59,300
I never disobeyed you?

502
00:33:59,427 --> 00:34:01,224
That's right.

503
00:34:02,739 --> 00:34:05,843
You used to be so sweet and obedient.

504
00:34:10,630 --> 00:34:13,300
But come to think of it, I like this rebellious side of you too.

505
00:34:14,875 --> 00:34:15,876
Hey,

506
00:34:16,491 --> 00:34:19,400
when are we finally going to have some wild fun again?

507
00:34:22,830 --> 00:34:24,589
I haven't really been in the mood lately.

508
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:28,240
You know I'm getting fired at the end of this month, right?

509
00:34:28,768 --> 00:34:30,400
If you can't help me,

510
00:34:31,014 --> 00:34:32,440
then you'll just have to take care of yourself.

511
00:34:33,190 --> 00:34:34,240
Oh, come on, Ta!

512
00:34:34,387 --> 00:34:37,320
I've been taking care of myself so much my hand's practically peeling.

513
00:34:40,590 --> 00:34:42,250
I think it's getting rubbed raw.

514
00:34:51,900 --> 00:34:52,901
He's here.

515
00:34:53,648 --> 00:34:55,500
- Good morning, Toey!
- Good morning, Toey!

516
00:34:55,600 --> 00:34:58,891
Let me carry that for you. Watch your step.

517
00:34:58,939 --> 00:35:00,278
Careful not to trip.

518
00:35:00,342 --> 00:35:02,840
Here are the documents you need to sign today.

519
00:35:02,907 --> 00:35:05,708
I've organized everything neatly in here for you.

520
00:35:05,787 --> 00:35:07,440
Just open it up, and they're ready to sign.

521
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:09,520
This way, please. Watch your step. Careful not to trip.

522
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:13,840
- Hey, old lady!
- Huh?

523
00:35:14,120 --> 00:35:15,321
Aren't we going to do anything?

524
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:19,120
Look at those bitches!

525
00:35:19,140 --> 00:35:21,536
They've already started sucking up to him like crazy.

526
00:35:22,448 --> 00:35:23,664
Don't pay them any attention, Sak.

527
00:35:24,112 --> 00:35:26,438
We're both valuable employees.

528
00:35:26,859 --> 00:35:30,120
We work hard and earn every baht of taxpayers' money.

529
00:35:30,860 --> 00:35:32,987
There's no way Toey will fire us.

530
00:35:34,824 --> 00:35:35,825
This color is pretty, isn't it?

531
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:37,760
- It really complements my skin tone.
- It's gorgeous!

532
00:35:39,147 --> 00:35:42,400
Hey, Hong, aren't you going to try to impress him too?

533
00:35:42,891 --> 00:35:45,500
You're the youngest here. You might be the first to go.

534
00:35:47,563 --> 00:35:51,832
I'm confident I've always worked hard and done my best.

535
00:35:52,894 --> 00:35:55,600
I'm sure Toey will recognize my dedication.

536
00:35:56,419 --> 00:35:57,840
Don't worry.

537
00:35:58,752 --> 00:35:59,796
You're under my wing.

538
00:36:00,424 --> 00:36:02,632
I've already told Toey not to fire you.

539
00:36:05,678 --> 00:36:07,300
Thank you so much, ma'am.

540
00:36:18,667 --> 00:36:20,688
But I feel so sorry for you.

541
00:36:21,942 --> 00:36:24,080
Who could be so cruel

542
00:36:24,406 --> 00:36:28,840
as to tell you about her affair with the Director?

543
00:36:29,752 --> 00:36:34,110
Otherwise, you wouldn't be getting pushed out like this.

544
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:37,592
It must be someone right here in this office.

545
00:36:37,950 --> 00:36:40,320
Who knows? It might even be you, Hong.

546
00:36:41,539 --> 00:36:42,540
Ta!

547
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:45,960
Why would you say that?

548
00:36:47,294 --> 00:36:50,720
You know how much I adore you.

549
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:54,101
I'm just kidding.

550
00:36:56,195 --> 00:36:57,196
Ta!

551
00:37:23,558 --> 00:37:26,720
I got up early this morning to prepare all the documents.

552
00:37:27,243 --> 00:37:30,440
- This way, Toey!
- Whisky, open the door!

553
00:37:30,616 --> 00:37:32,640
- After you, Toey!
- Please, Toey!

554
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:36,070
- Welcome, Toey!
- Welcome, Toey!

555
00:37:36,088 --> 00:37:37,464
Your coffee, Toey.

556
00:37:37,502 --> 00:37:39,000
And your salad.

557
00:37:40,901 --> 00:37:41,902
Hey!

558
00:37:43,317 --> 00:37:45,200
Instead of wasting time sucking up to him,

559
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:49,520
why don't you focus on doing some actual work and proving your worth?

560
00:37:51,267 --> 00:37:53,043
Go on! Get back to work!

561
00:37:54,979 --> 00:37:57,920
Or I'll report you to Mrs. Nopnapha.

562
00:38:00,878 --> 00:38:02,200
Ugh, the coffee will just have to go.

563
00:38:04,486 --> 00:38:05,487
Toey.

564
00:38:06,544 --> 00:38:09,675
I'm not the other person getting fired, am I?

565
00:38:10,182 --> 00:38:11,608
I can't tell you that yet.

566
00:38:12,183 --> 00:38:13,190
I'm still evaluating everyone.

567
00:38:13,626 --> 00:38:14,925
I'll make my decision at the end of the month.

568
00:38:15,576 --> 00:38:17,920
But I'm next in line to take over your position.

569
00:38:19,086 --> 00:38:21,720
If you fire me, who's going to succeed you?

570
00:38:22,126 --> 00:38:23,127
Sak, of course.

571
00:38:23,646 --> 00:38:25,667
He's been here almost as long as you have.

572
00:38:25,971 --> 00:38:27,520
And his performance is just as good as yours.

573
00:38:28,446 --> 00:38:31,280
That King Kong-sized queen? As good as me?

574
00:38:32,878 --> 00:38:35,320
When it comes to document formatting and page margins,

575
00:38:35,688 --> 00:38:39,480
I guarantee no one in this entire ministry is as meticulous as me!

576
00:38:40,678 --> 00:38:43,440
But Sak is also really good at making perfectly neat pleats in tablecloths.

577
00:38:52,395 --> 00:38:54,155
Phorn, what are you doing?

578
00:39:02,582 --> 00:39:03,583
Toey.

579
00:39:07,531 --> 00:39:10,920
I'm showing you another one of my special talents.

580
00:39:11,840 --> 00:39:13,320
Just for you, Toey.

581
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:20,201
Toey.

582
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:26,001
Has the pickled shellfish you ordered from your mom arrived yet?

583
00:39:26,123 --> 00:39:27,480
It should arrive tomorrow.

584
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:30,101
So what are you selling these days?

585
00:39:32,547 --> 00:39:34,080
Ta.

586
00:39:35,038 --> 00:39:36,840
Since you're leaving at the end of the month,

587
00:39:37,379 --> 00:39:39,550
you might as well do some work before you go.

588
00:39:40,430 --> 00:39:41,431
Here.

589
00:39:42,552 --> 00:39:45,560
Once you're done, put it on my desk.

590
00:39:47,715 --> 00:39:51,000
Uncle Somsak, do you know what report I'm drafting?

591
00:39:52,323 --> 00:39:54,680
No. How would I know?

592
00:39:54,878 --> 00:39:56,723
Your work isn't my responsibility.

593
00:39:57,315 --> 00:40:00,080
It's a report on all the pointless things our department does.

594
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:04,040
Every day, we convert paper documents into digital files,

595
00:40:04,539 --> 00:40:06,480
then print those digital files back onto paper.

596
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:09,880
The content stays the same. Only the date changes.

597
00:40:10,094 --> 00:40:11,920
Then we run around getting signatures from everyone in the Ministry,

598
00:40:12,350 --> 00:40:13,520
before filing everything away again.

599
00:40:14,798 --> 00:40:16,520
I'm sending this report straight to the Prime Minister.

600
00:40:16,995 --> 00:40:18,800
Maybe it'll finally bring about some changes.

601
00:40:21,192 --> 00:40:24,824
Sure. Good luck with your little revolution!

602
00:40:25,310 --> 00:40:28,403
Millions of people have probably had the same idea.

603
00:40:28,734 --> 00:40:30,320
But this is the civil service.

604
00:40:30,500 --> 00:40:33,840
We've been doing things this way since you were still a sperm cell.

605
00:40:34,051 --> 00:40:37,704
And we'll keep doing it until the end of the world.

606
00:40:41,520 --> 00:40:45,600
Listen here, Mutta.

607
00:40:45,768 --> 00:40:50,440
You're already in the final days of your civil service career.

608
00:40:50,966 --> 00:40:52,320
Just get on with it.

609
00:40:52,367 --> 00:40:56,022
Type away, take it easy, and do the bare minimum.

610
00:40:56,200 --> 00:40:59,500
Before you know it, it'll be 2 p.m. Time to put on your makeup and go home.

611
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,040
Why make life so complicated, right?

612
00:41:02,448 --> 00:41:03,449
Exactly.

613
00:41:04,118 --> 00:41:08,360
Mutta, you're lucky you actually have work to do.

614
00:41:08,752 --> 00:41:10,840
Look at the two of us.

615
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:15,560
We've been filing our nails so much our fingers are about to fall off.

616
00:41:20,758 --> 00:41:22,920
Thank you, Cha-am, for pointing out the problem.

617
00:41:23,083 --> 00:41:26,700
Now I can include overstaffing in my report too.

618
00:41:27,526 --> 00:41:30,840
Actually, laying off just two people probably isn't enough.

619
00:41:31,216 --> 00:41:34,840
They should get rid of half the staff to stop wasting taxpayers' money.

620
00:41:36,900 --> 00:41:38,901
Who's got nothing to do?

621
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:41,120
Look! I'm reusing paper!

622
00:41:41,648 --> 00:41:42,649
See?

623
00:41:42,939 --> 00:41:44,500
Cha-am, get over here and help me!

624
00:41:45,451 --> 00:41:48,600
And I am busy making photocopies too.

625
00:41:50,824 --> 00:41:53,966
Ta, I'll take care of these documents for you.

626
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:56,200
I'm trying to prove how hardworking I am.

627
00:41:59,832 --> 00:42:02,920
Hong, would you like to take some of this work?

628
00:42:03,347 --> 00:42:06,942
No, thanks. I've always been dedicated to my work.

629
00:42:07,336 --> 00:42:10,414
I'm sure the Ministry will recognize my hard work.

630
00:42:11,337 --> 00:42:12,338
Fine, I'll do it myself.

631
00:42:26,606 --> 00:42:29,515
Hey, have you ever stumbled upon any of your dad's secrets?

632
00:42:31,323 --> 00:42:34,520
You mean his mistress? Dad never tried to hide that.

633
00:42:34,790 --> 00:42:36,191
So I wouldn't really call it a secret.

634
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:49,040
What about secrets between your dad and his mistress?

635
00:42:50,134 --> 00:42:51,200
I have no idea.

636
00:42:51,435 --> 00:42:53,200
That homewrecking bitch works for my dad.

637
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:56,300
If they have any secrets, they're probably hidden at work.

638
00:42:56,715 --> 00:42:59,520
You mean in your dad's office?

639
00:43:00,358 --> 00:43:02,400
Yeah. I've never snooped around in there.

640
00:43:02,814 --> 00:43:04,500
Why do you ask? You sound like a detective.

641
00:43:04,776 --> 00:43:07,438
Oh, I'm investigating my dad's mistress.

642
00:43:07,656 --> 00:43:09,960
I want to know where adults hide their secrets.

643
00:43:17,875 --> 00:43:19,040
What's that noise?

644
00:43:24,027 --> 00:43:25,963
Hey! What's that noise?

645
00:43:28,992 --> 00:43:30,440
Is there a fire, everyone?

646
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,601
Let's get out of here!

647
00:43:32,620 --> 00:43:35,200
Hey, it's just another fire drill. No need to run.

648
00:43:35,486 --> 00:43:38,160
But we didn't get any notice about a fire drill.

649
00:43:38,238 --> 00:43:40,440
Fire! Fire!

650
00:43:42,339 --> 00:43:43,640
The fire escape is this way, Uncle!

651
00:43:46,038 --> 00:43:48,640
Everyone, the other departments are already evacuating!

652
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:50,001
Then let's get moving!

653
00:43:52,520 --> 00:43:54,520
But I haven't finished making photocopies!

654
00:43:55,515 --> 00:43:57,240
Then take them with you, you idiot!

655
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:13,180
Fine, I'll just leave them!

656
00:44:43,400 --> 00:44:45,401
[Browsing History: Assassin]

657
00:44:45,501 --> 00:44:46,502
[No results found]

658
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:51,921
[Contract Killing: 1 result found]

659
00:45:16,696 --> 00:45:19,320
Who the hell put us on the 21st floor?

660
00:45:19,672 --> 00:45:21,520
Why couldn't they put us on the third?

661
00:45:21,621 --> 00:45:23,459
Hey, you lot!

662
00:45:24,264 --> 00:45:25,598
Why didn't any of you wait for me?

663
00:45:25,650 --> 00:45:27,880
Where the hell have you been, old lady?

664
00:45:27,900 --> 00:45:29,651
And look at you! Why are you such a mess?

665
00:45:30,179 --> 00:45:32,126
Hey, are you staring at my boobs?

666
00:45:32,595 --> 00:45:33,320
How disgusting!

667
00:45:33,566 --> 00:45:35,320
I was running down the fire escape.

668
00:45:35,344 --> 00:45:38,000
Things just started falling off with every exhausting flight of stairs.

669
00:45:38,163 --> 00:45:42,540
So, does everyone see the importance of fire insurance now?

670
00:45:42,894 --> 00:45:44,320
Let's sign up right now.

671
00:45:44,387 --> 00:45:47,262
I'm determined to sell at least eight policies today.

672
00:45:47,448 --> 00:45:49,049
You're still trying to sell insurance?

673
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:50,920
Is everyone okay?

674
00:45:52,475 --> 00:45:55,400
Veekit, I ran all the way down.

675
00:45:55,579 --> 00:45:57,280
My legs are completely weak.

676
00:45:57,936 --> 00:45:59,670
Where's Ta? Where is she?

677
00:46:00,016 --> 00:46:01,080
Has anyone seen Ta?

678
00:46:01,411 --> 00:46:06,000
Oh, I saw her leave the office a while before the alarm went off.

679
00:46:06,142 --> 00:46:09,040
Maybe she's already downstairs with another group.

680
00:46:09,760 --> 00:46:12,920
You seem awfully worried about Ta, Veekit.

681
00:46:13,038 --> 00:46:15,240
Almost like you're husband and wife.

682
00:46:15,260 --> 00:46:17,261
Hey! Slap yourself across the mouth right now.

683
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:20,520
How could she be the nephew's wife when she's already the uncle's mistress?
Disgusting!

684
00:46:21,278 --> 00:46:23,584
Wait, is everyone here?

685
00:46:23,700 --> 00:46:24,701
Oh, right!

686
00:46:25,147 --> 00:46:28,870
Apart from Ta, is anyone else missing?

687
00:46:29,920 --> 00:46:32,560
Toey! Toey must still be upstairs!

688
00:46:34,272 --> 00:46:35,820
The photocopier!

689
00:46:38,438 --> 00:46:39,439
Ta!

690
00:46:40,763 --> 00:46:43,000
Toey must have fainted upstairs.

691
00:46:43,064 --> 00:46:45,360
I'll go rescue him myself.

692
00:46:45,502 --> 00:46:48,110
Stop right there! You're just going up to rescue Toey to score points with him!

693
00:46:48,200 --> 00:46:50,801
You think someone in your condition can carry Toey downstairs?

694
00:46:50,894 --> 00:46:53,726
No way! You're old as hell, you hag!

695
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:55,440
Hey, stop it! Don't underestimate me!

696
00:46:55,452 --> 00:46:57,400
I do aerobics at Lumpini Park every day!

697
00:46:57,453 --> 00:47:00,200
You? How strong can you possibly be? Let's see what you've got!

698
00:47:00,220 --> 00:47:01,640
There! I thought you did aerobics at Lumpini Park!

699
00:47:01,660 --> 00:47:04,360
- You wanna fight, you bitch?
- Come on, then! Show me how strong you are!

700
00:47:04,395 --> 00:47:06,320
Come at me! Come on, you old hag!

701
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:08,561
- Come on, you old hag! Bring it!
- Uncle Sak!

702
00:47:08,600 --> 00:47:09,601
Auntie Phorn!

703
00:47:09,686 --> 00:47:10,687
- What?
- What?

704
00:47:11,824 --> 00:47:13,440
Everyone's already gone.

705
00:47:13,518 --> 00:47:14,519
Huh?

706
00:47:14,792 --> 00:47:16,360
- Toey!
- Toey!

707
00:47:17,280 --> 00:47:18,480
Toey!

708
00:47:19,368 --> 00:47:23,550
Oh, why did those idiots even run back upstairs?

709
00:48:10,896 --> 00:48:12,880
Oh my God, Toey!

710
00:48:13,097 --> 00:48:14,680
Are you okay, Toey?

711
00:48:14,696 --> 00:48:15,697
Come on.

712
00:48:16,400 --> 00:48:17,401
Let me help you.

713
00:48:18,467 --> 00:48:20,250
Wait, wait. I'm not that bad.

714
00:48:20,728 --> 00:48:23,160
My blood sugar's low, my blood pressure's high,

715
00:48:23,230 --> 00:48:26,060
my asthma's acting up, and I'm having a panic attack.

716
00:48:26,131 --> 00:48:28,560
Okay, then. Let me help you. Come on.

717
00:48:28,718 --> 00:48:30,400
Get over here, you idiots! Hurry!

718
00:48:32,398 --> 00:48:33,560
Toey, are you okay?

719
00:48:35,347 --> 00:48:36,880
- Can you manage?
- One, two, three!

720
00:48:37,870 --> 00:48:40,200
- I'm scared!
- One, two, three!

721
00:48:42,190 --> 00:48:43,347
That's enough! Stop!

722
00:48:44,413 --> 00:48:46,040
You idiots are no help at all!

723
00:48:46,158 --> 00:48:47,800
Come here! Move aside! I'll do it myself!

724
00:48:48,760 --> 00:48:49,761
Get out of the way, you old hag!

725
00:48:50,568 --> 00:48:53,600
Toey! Toey! Come on!

726
00:48:53,710 --> 00:48:55,720
Let me help you, Toey.

727
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:57,001
Thank you so much, Sak.

728
00:49:00,310 --> 00:49:01,320
I'll go ahead, then.

729
00:49:09,923 --> 00:49:11,520
Who the hell slashed my tires?

730
00:49:11,608 --> 00:49:14,309
Meow! She deliberately sabotaged you!

731
00:49:14,533 --> 00:49:15,534
Meow!

732
00:49:15,942 --> 00:49:18,800
You lying old hag! You're the one who stabbed Uncle Sak in the back!

733
00:49:18,843 --> 00:49:22,080
Uncle? Who are you calling Uncle? You deserve a slap!

734
00:49:24,342 --> 00:49:27,400
Toey, since you're about to be burned alive anyway,

735
00:49:27,622 --> 00:49:28,886
please just tell us

736
00:49:29,147 --> 00:49:31,720
who the other person getting fired is!

737
00:49:34,982 --> 00:49:36,400
Stop! Stop right there!

738
00:49:36,598 --> 00:49:38,280
I'm not telling anyone who it is

739
00:49:38,662 --> 00:49:41,560
- until you all help me first!
- Chuenchom!

740
00:49:41,744 --> 00:49:43,493
Go find something to wheel Toey out on!

741
00:49:45,230 --> 00:49:46,231
Everyone!

742
00:49:46,632 --> 00:49:48,320
What the hell do you need that for?

743
00:50:03,486 --> 00:50:04,887
Wait, wait!

744
00:50:08,462 --> 00:50:11,480
Now I realize just how much you all love me.

745
00:50:13,304 --> 00:50:14,880
I'll resign myself

746
00:50:16,160 --> 00:50:17,861
so everyone else can keep their jobs.

747
00:50:24,288 --> 00:50:27,560
Everyone! The fire escape is this way!

748
00:50:35,384 --> 00:50:37,400
Toey!

749
00:51:24,155 --> 00:51:25,156
Ta.

750
00:51:25,371 --> 00:51:26,372
Veekit.

751
00:51:33,864 --> 00:51:34,865
What are you doing in here?

752
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:40,441
[Hong]

753
00:51:47,056 --> 00:51:48,960
You've known about the Director and Hong all along, haven't you?

754
00:52:08,854 --> 00:52:09,855
Hong!

755
00:52:10,816 --> 00:52:11,817
Wait!

756
00:52:12,779 --> 00:52:14,500
I know everything about you and the Director.

757
00:52:14,667 --> 00:52:17,560
Ta, you can't tell anyone about this!

758
00:52:17,696 --> 00:52:19,643
I'm begging you, Ta!

759
00:52:19,915 --> 00:52:22,120
From now on, you'll have to help me with my work

760
00:52:22,539 --> 00:52:23,920
whenever I need you.

761
00:52:25,606 --> 00:52:26,779
She's pregnant.

762
00:52:27,083 --> 00:52:30,160
- How the hell is that possible?
- Because you slept with her!

763
00:52:30,696 --> 00:52:31,840
Ta, are you really pregnant?

764
00:52:32,280 --> 00:52:33,281
Yes.

765
00:52:33,694 --> 00:52:35,320
But I'm not having an abortion.

766
00:52:36,323 --> 00:52:37,560
I'm keeping the baby.

767
00:52:41,827 --> 00:52:43,600
- No, no!
- Get her!
